prompts.prompt:
Write a Verilog module named `iir10_v2`, an order-10 IIR filter with inputs `clk`, active-low `rst_n`, an 8-bit unsigned sample input `x`, and a 16-bit registered output `y`. Each cycle compute y[n] = (sum over k=0..10 of B[k]*x[n-k]) + ((9*y[n-1])>>4) + ((5*y[n-2])>>4), keeping only the low 16 bits (mod 2^16), where the feedforward coefficients are B = [20, 38, 62, 60, 30, 6, 18, 43, 22, 30, 45] (B[0] applies to the current sample) and y[n-1], y[n-2] are the previous two outputs. Clear all state to 0 on `!rst_n`.

Use exactly this module interface (port names and widths must match):

module iir10_v2 (
  input clk, input rst_n, input [7:0] x, output reg [15:0] y
);

Write standard synthesizable Verilog-2001. Active-low rst_n clears the outputs; outputs are registered on posedge clk.

prompts.reference_rtl:
// Order-10 IIR, ONE combinational sum over all taps + feedback (the long
// path grows with the order -> lower Fmax; restructure to go faster).
module iir10_v2 (
  input clk, input rst_n, input [7:0] x, output reg [15:0] y
);
  reg [7:0] xd1;
  reg [7:0] xd2;
  reg [7:0] xd3;
  reg [7:0] xd4;
  reg [7:0] xd5;
  reg [7:0] xd6;
  reg [7:0] xd7;
  reg [7:0] xd8;
  reg [7:0] xd9;
  reg [7:0] xd10;
  reg [15:0] y2;
  wire [31:0] acc = 20*x + 38*xd1 + 62*xd2 + 60*xd3 + 30*xd4 + 6*xd5 + 18*xd6 + 43*xd7 + 22*xd8 + 30*xd9 + 45*xd10 + ((9*y)>>4) + ((5*y2)>>4);
  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (!rst_n) begin y<=0; y2<=0; xd1<=0; xd2<=0; xd3<=0; xd4<=0; xd5<=0; xd6<=0; xd7<=0; xd8<=0; xd9<=0; xd10<=0; end
    else begin
      y <= acc[15:0];
      y2 <= y;
      xd10<=xd9; xd9<=xd8; xd8<=xd7; xd7<=xd6; xd6<=xd5; xd5<=xd4; xd4<=xd3; xd3<=xd2; xd2<=xd1; xd1 <= x;
    end
  end
endmodule

